.TH "ROARK\-DASHBOARD\-WIDGET\-CREATE" "1" "" "roark-dashboard-widget-create" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-dashboard\-widget\-create \- Add a widget
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark dashboard widget create
\fIdashboard\-id\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Adds a widget to the top of a dashboard. Its name must be unique on the dashboard.
.SH "API"
POST /v1/dashboard/{dashboardId}/widget
.SH "ARGUMENTS"
.TP
\fIdashboard\-id\fR
The dashboard ID
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-measures\fR \fI<value>\fR
What to aggregate: 1 to 10 measures. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-filters\fR \fI<value>\fR
Applied to every measure, on top of each measure's own filters. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-interval\fR \fI<value>\fR
Bucket size. Defaults from the window's length and steps coarser when the window would exceed 500 buckets. One of: HOUR, DAY, WEEK, MONTH. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-comparison\-mode\fR \fI<value>\fR
PREVIOUS_PERIOD adds the preceding window of the same length to every series. One of: NONE, PREVIOUS_PERIOD. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-comparison\-groups\fR \fI<value>\fR
Run every measure once per named filter set, e.g. one group per agent. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<value>\fR
Unique on the dashboard: how the widget is matched on update. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<value>\fR
Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-display\fR \fI<value>\fR
Chart type. Defaults to LINE. One of: LINE, NUMBER, RADAR, STACKED_BAR, TABLE. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-size\fR \fI<value>\fR
Grid width. Defaults to MEDIUM. One of: SMALL, MEDIUM, LARGE, EXTRA_LARGE. Optional.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<json>\fR
Request body as JSON, or @file to read one (@\- for stdin).
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-input\fR
Never prompt; fail instead.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
API base URL.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<token>\fR
Bearer token. Prefer ROARK_API_BEARER_TOKEN or the stored credential.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR \fI<count>\fR
Retries for retryable failures.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output format: auto, json, jsonl, plain.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Shorthand for \-\-format json.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable colour.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
